---
code: wrapper-peel-incoherent
when-fires: a wrapper's `__predict` and `__lend_map` disagree on the peel tail position. oracle/validate.rs peel_and_entry_coherence. Spanned (the predict name_span).
why: 273 §5 (declarations-genuinely-contradict): a pre-network fail-fast. The holes are typed: `{wrapper}` plus the two disagreeing depths.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
error[wrapper-peel-incoherent]: Wrapper `sudo`'s `__predict` and `__lend_map`
disagree on where the guest begins: `__predict` reaches `"$@"` after 1 argv
token(s), `__lend_map` after 0, so the guest would start at a different token
depending on which member dispatched, and Dorc stops before contacting any host.
Fix whichever argparse is wrong so both members peel to the same tail.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: wrapper-peel-incoherent
{{wrapper}} = "sudo"
{{predict_depth}} = "1"
{{lend_map_depth}} = "0"
